cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "No fertility refund: speculative-decoding acceptance across 21 languages (data and code)"
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
version: "1.0"
authors:
  - given-names: Hanyu
    family-names: Yang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0419-4070"
abstract: >-
  Per-item speculative-decoding acceptance for two built-in self-drafters (Qwen3.5-9B MTP, Gemma 4 E4B
  assistant) on 200 FLORES-200 sentences in each of 21 languages, with the code that measures it. Under
  decision rules stated by the author before the runs (not independently verifiable; one gate amendment
  followed the first run), every gate passed and both kill rules fired in both families on their point
  estimates: acceptance does not rise with tokenizer fertility (it falls in Gemma and is flat in Qwen),
  and because every other language has lower acceptance length than English, the refund fraction is
  negative wherever it is defined. Qwen's half of the verdict rests on point estimates whose
  language-bootstrap intervals cross the thresholds.
keywords:
  - speculative decoding
  - multi-token prediction
  - tokenizer fertility
  - multilingual inference
  - FLORES-200
  - negative result
license:
